<title>NEW ZEALAND: Most NZ ADRs flat or down as Dow backs up.</title>
<headline>Most NZ ADRs flat or down as Dow backs up.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs with the exception of Tranz Rail were flat or down as the Dow backed up 8.2 points to 5996.58 in late Wednesday trade.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	 Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$26 5/8	 -0 1/2</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$26 3/8	 nil</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$20	     nil</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$15 7/8	 -0 1/4</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$81 1/2	 -0 3/8</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$14 1/2	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  36		  -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  64		 untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  241 1/2	   +0 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  155		 -1 3/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  138 1/2	   -1 1/4</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.15	    -3</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.49	    -2</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$3.10	    -2</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
